# Browser-visible configuration.
#
# The operations-console URL is intentionally NOT a VITE_* value. The Worker
# serves the console shell only at /console/<ADMIN_PATH>, where ADMIN_PATH is a
# server-side secret. Reading the client bundle reveals only the /console/
# prefix, never the secret suffix.
#
# There are currently no browser-visible environment variables.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side secrets — NEVER put these in a VITE_* variable.
#
# Local development: put them in .dev.vars (gitignored).
# Production: `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ADMIN_SETUP_TOKEN
#   One-time token that allows POST /api/setup/admin to create the first
#   administrator. Remove it after setup; the endpoint also refuses to run once
#   any admin exists.
#
# IP_PEPPER
#   Server-side pepper used when hashing client IPs for rate limiting and audit
#   records. The raw IP is never stored.
#
# ADMIN_PATH
#   Secret suffix for the operations console: /console/<ADMIN_PATH>. Use a long
#   random value (for example `ops-` plus `openssl rand -hex 24`). If unset, all
#   /console/* requests return 404.
#
# All values should be long random strings.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY is no longer used by this application. It may be removed.
